From 8fa4c559a0d445367bad5fb06343624d5ebfbe14 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DaffyDabz <daffydabz@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 23:29:09 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 055/371] client: the map teleport works again, on land and
 from a ship's wheel at sea

Picking an island on the map always failed, on land and at sea. At sea
the bot read "Sorry, you can't teleport while captaining a privateer
ship." on a normal ship; on land the game said he had no teleport
token for an island he had one for.

The pirate's teleport flags each carry a check: the map sets "no
island token" with the island check, boarding a ship sets "on ship",
"not same crew" and "siege captain" with the ship's checks. A flag
blocks only when its check says no. setTeleportFlags stored each check
under its loop key and then shifted that key in place (b >>= 1 changes
a BitMask32 itself), so the stored key changed under the dict and the
next unset bit popped it. No check ever survived, and every such flag
blocked outright. The loop now makes a new key each step.

The two "next flag to check" helpers also masked the pirate's own flags
in place (flags &= ...), dropping "on ship", "not same crew", "ignore"
and "in welcome world" from them on every check, so a pirate who had
checked once looked like he was on land to a friend teleporting to
him. They now work on a copy.

Offline replay of the real methods (8 cases: own ship, land with and
without a token, privateer captain, in battle, teleport to him on his
ship, leaving the ship): the old code fails 5, the new code passes all.

Client file only (pirates/pirate/DistributedPlayerPirate.py), no server
restart. An old client still cannot use the map teleport.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 pirates/pirate/DistributedPlayerPirate.py | 13 ++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/pirates/pirate/DistributedPlayerPirate.py b/pirates/pirate/DistributedPlayerPirate.py
index ef92b2f..cf8ebac 100644
--- a/pirates/pirate/DistributedPlayerPirate.py
+++ b/pirates/pirate/DistributedPlayerPirate.py
@@ -1016,14 +1016,14 @@ class DistributedPlayerPirate(DistributedPirateBase, DistributedPlayer, Distribu
 
     def getNextTeleportConfirmFlag(self, currentFlag=None, flags=None):
         currentFlag = currentFlag or BitMask32()
-        flags = flags or self.teleportFlags
-        flags &= PiratesGlobals.TFNoTeleportOut
+        # family server (11-16): & makes a new mask; &= changed the pirate's own flags in place, stripping TFOnShip,
+        # TFNotSameCrew, TFIgnore and TFInWelcomeWorld from them on every check
+        flags = (flags or self.teleportFlags) & PiratesGlobals.TFNoTeleportOut
         return flags.keepNextHighestBit(currentFlag)
 
     def getNextTeleportToConfirmFlag(self, currentFlag=None, flags=None):
         currentFlag = currentFlag or BitMask32()
-        flags = flags or self.teleportFlags
-        flags &= PiratesGlobals.TFNoTeleportTo
+        flags = (flags or self.teleportFlags) & PiratesGlobals.TFNoTeleportTo
         return flags.keepNextHighestBit(currentFlag)
 
     def getNoTeleportString(self, flag=None):
@@ -1101,7 +1101,10 @@ class DistributedPlayerPirate(DistributedPirateBase, DistributedPlayer, Distribu
             elif b in confirmDict:
                 self.teleportConfirmCallbacks[b] = confirmDict[b]
 
-            b >>= 1
+            # family server (11-16): a new mask each step. b >>= 1 shifted the key just stored in place, so the
+            # next unset bit popped it and no flag's check survived: every flag that should ask first (an island
+            # teleport token, being on a ship, captaining a privateer) blocked the teleport outright
+            b = b >> 1
 
     def getTeleportFlags(self):
         return self.teleportFlags
